From 113840c02c3ebde7ddbad21b953aa610be81e144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:05:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/57] MAS local: never upload crash reports

Not for upstream: it is the opposite of the upstream design.

Uploads used to depend on the consent provider: -metrics-collection,
-crash-report-mode always, or a saved crashReportPreference of 1 (Qt
settings, registry key HKCU\Software\Android Open Source
Project\Emulator\set) all gave ALWAYS, and the reports were then sent to
Google. This build keeps reports on the machine only, whatever the
options and settings say:

- crashpad_handler is started without an upload URL, so it never starts
  its upload thread;
- uploadEntries() no longer consults the consent provider (no dialog),
  forces uploads off in the database settings and only keeps the newest
  reports locally, as with no consent before;
- ProcessPendingReport() refuses without touching the report or the
  network, and crashreport -u refuses before recording an upload
  request.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:Claude-Opus-5.5
Change-Id: I53b681b12f1830aa75fdd4d3dc6d0be167e6ee98
